$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488260 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068732 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e0c15b8-dc6e-570d-9392-4c679395cc87" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Equation by Changing the Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fd3c8d2-c437-5775-8892-990be1d8c600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fd3c8d2-c437-5775-8892-990be1d8c600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487789} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd615eb-4925-5039-bbc3-b187bac64900" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5891ca3-f381-532b-913f-b6dc3bcab055" :question/math-academy-id "q-223145" :question/problem "If ${4}^{x}=\\frac{1}{4},$ then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $\\frac{1}{4}$ as ${4}^{-1}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{x} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {4}^{x} & ={4}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(4)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{x} & ={4}^{-1} \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068732 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e0c15b8-dc6e-570d-9392-4c679395cc87" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Equation by Changing the Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2e01ff2-d747-5b9e-b936-49bec7a790ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2e01ff2-d747-5b9e-b936-49bec7a790ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487906} :answer-field/id #uuid "61d05db5-0e4d-5d3d-9a30-6426013fad19" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa2ae142-bf31-5242-a307-d8faa66809d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-223149" :question/problem "If ${6}^{t}=\\frac{1}{36},$ then $t=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $36$ as ${6}^{2}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{t} & =\\frac{1}{36} \\\\ {6}^{t} & =\\frac{1}{{6}^{2}} \\\\ {6}^{t} & ={6}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(6)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{t} & ={6}^{-2} \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "368d83db-e01e-543b-ba45-8fc9c63242e9" :knowledge-point/title "Rearranging and Solving an Exponential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf7b7247-c19a-5409-86f4-f0606135b5c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf7b7247-c19a-5409-86f4-f0606135b5c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487926} :answer-field/id #uuid "72c56336-2a3e-5cd0-b70e-c6cad4b4b776" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82072348-e506-5a54-8f29-a9a2b212c19f" :question/math-academy-id "q-223185" :question/problem "If $2\\cdot {6}^{k}=72,$ then $k=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by dividing both sides by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {6}^{k} & =72 \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot {6}^{k}}{2} & =\\frac{72}{2} \\\\ {6}^{k} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite $36$ as ${6}^{2}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{k} & =36 \\\\ {6}^{k} & ={6}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(6)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{k} & ={6}^{2} \\\\ k & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1e0a7d0-f891-5f5f-8d8d-1ced62b2899e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e9d58b-292d-554b-975c-09e6d6f27473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487596} {:answer/id #uuid "1c905a9a-15d4-590b-b106-bf7966bb52c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487625} {:answer/id #uuid "4810e6de-00c2-58a4-b292-33b27495778a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487706} {:answer/id #uuid "7b65fa77-cf93-5771-9fcd-8ca54e7b60b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487807} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b8a081-634d-5fc1-82ee-3b4f8cbcd510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=20" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218648